# Publish refreshed data to GitHub Pages

GitHub Pages is the primary place the user views results. Do **not** start or restart a local `http.server` for this project unless the user explicitly asks.

After any scan, dashboard rebuild, or other update that changes viewing results:

1. Commit the refreshed outputs (dashboard HTML, compiled JSON, markdown, scan meta) when the user asked for a refresh/update, or when they asked to push.
2. Push to **both** remotes so the live site updates:
   - `public` → https://github.com/PNelsonFTP/illinois-property-scanner (GitHub Pages)
   - `origin` → https://github.com/PNelsonFTP/distressed-property-scanner (private mirror)
3. Confirm Pages is serving the new scan when relevant:
   - Live site: https://pnelsonftp.github.io/illinois-property-scanner/
   - Dashboard: https://pnelsonftp.github.io/illinois-property-scanner/dashboard/distressed-property-dashboard.html
4. Tell the user the **GitHub Pages** URL is updated — not a local `127.0.0.1:8000` link.

Do not add auto-start logic to `scan.py` or other application code for a local web server.
